{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 37, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "Hark forth dear traveler to lands where cherry blossoms do dance and tea is sipped with grace most grand. Let us weave thee a journey most splendid across the isles of Nippon where honor and enchantment intertwine.\n\nUpon thine first morn do thou set foot in Tokyo the bustling metropolis where neon lights do waltz with lanterns old. To the temple of Senso-ji thou shalt repair where incense fills the air and prayers to the gods do ascend. Marvel at the throats of Asakusa where vendors cry their wares and street food doth tempt thy taste.\n\nOn the morrow do thou venture forth to the district of Shibuya where scramble crosses hearts of lions do watch with solemn gaze. In the shrine of Meiji thou shalt find solace where torii gates beckon thee through forests sacred. Let not thy steps falter when thou standest at the peak of Mount Fuji for though distant still thou seest her majesty in misty hues.\n\nTo Kyoto thou shalt journey where time doth linger like a samurai’s blade. In the golden pavilion do thou tread where reflections shimmer upon waters still. Walk the paths of Arashiyama where bamboo groves do whisper secrets ancient and temples cling to cliffs with quiet dignity.\n\nIn Nara let thee lose thyself amongst deer who bow with gentle grace and in Osaka do taste takoyaki till thy heart be satisfied. To Hiroshima thou shalt bear witness where peace doth bloom amidst the ruins of a time most grim. Stand in solemn silence at Miyajima and gaze upon the torii that floats upon waters serene.\n\nLet thy final days find thee in Okinawa where turquoise waves do lap against shores of white. Behold the castle of Shuri where history doth hum through walls of stone. As thy voyage ends in Tokyo once more do thou feast on ramen rich and pray to gods who guard thy way.\n\nThus ends thy tale of Japan where every step is steeped in legend and each sight 